# Files the Ubuntu server executes must keep Unix line endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is `true` on the Windows machines this repository is developed on, and
# until this file existed nothing pinned the shell scripts. A fresh clone on Windows
# therefore checked them out with Windows line endings, and a shell script with a carriage
# return at the end of every line does not run on Ubuntu at all: bash stops on the second
# line with `$'\r': command not found`.
#
# That would break `deploy/free-disk.sh` — the script for recovering a server whose disk is
# full — at exactly the moment somebody needs it, and the error message says nothing about
# line endings. `tests/unit/test_invariant_deploy_disk_safety.py` fails if a carriage
# return reaches one of these files anyway.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
